@issuer = https://localhost:5001

### Public OIDC discovery document (must be anonymous and reachable by server-side validators)
GET {{issuer}}/.well-known/openid-configuration
Accept: application/json

### Public OIDC signing keys (public keys only)
GET {{issuer}}/.well-known/jwks
Accept: application/json

### Windows-authenticated development diagnostic (the VS Code REST Client does not send default Windows credentials)
### Expected: 401 in this client. Use scripts/test-identity-issuer.ps1 to verify the successful Windows-authenticated request.
GET {{issuer}}/diagnostics/windows-auth

### CSRF bootstrap (Windows Authentication required)
### Expected: 401 in this client. Successful response includes a request token; do not share its output.
GET {{issuer}}/csrf

### Session creation without Windows authentication or antiforgery token
### Expected: 401 for this client. An authenticated request without a token must return 400.
POST {{issuer}}/session
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Session refresh without Windows authentication or antiforgery token
### Expected: 401 for this client. An authenticated request without a token must return 400.
POST {{issuer}}/session/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Logout without Windows authentication or antiforgery token
### Expected: 401 for this client. An authenticated request without a token must return 400.
POST {{issuer}}/session/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Authorization endpoint requires Windows Authentication and a registered public client with PKCE
### The Windows-authenticated script follows the code redirect, validates ID/access tokens, and tests refresh rotation/replay without printing token values.
GET {{issuer}}/connect/authorize?client_id=dab-issuer-test-client&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5443%2Fcallback&response_type=code&scope=openid%20profile%20roles%20offline_access&state=manual-test&nonce=manual-test&code_challenge=replace-with-S256-challenge&code_challenge_method=S256

### Token endpoint requires a valid code and PKCE verifier; this incomplete request must return 400
POST {{issuer}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&client_id=dab-issuer-test-client&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5443%2Fcallback&code=invalid&code_verifier=invalid
